          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            between
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+duality"} Stone duality
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
          %p
            Given an
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideals"} ideals
            (typically defined as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernels"} kernels
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            of opens of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            The technical term for such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            one can canonically
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/locale#RelationToTopologicalSpaces"} extract a topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            produced in many classical Stone-type dualities. The points of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideals"} ideals
            corresponding to morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is often a particularly simple algebra. These often turn out to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+ideals"} maximal ideals
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Conversely, given a
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            of morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\to k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is often the “same”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            as above, only this time its underlying object is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
          %p
            Some examples from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+topology"} general topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
            = succeed "," do
