          %p
            The duality relevant to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+theory"} spectral theory
            is the duality between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+von+Neumann+algebras"} commutative von Neumann algebras
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/questions/20740/is-there-an-introduction-to-probability-theory-from-a-structuralist-categorical/20820#20820"} compact strictly localizable enhanced measurable spaces
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+operator"} normal operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            generates a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+von+Neumann+algebra"} commutative von Neumann algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            inside
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(H)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operators"} bounded operators
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi T
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi TT
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^*T=TT^*
            the algebra generated by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            will be noncommutative.)
          %p
            By the cited duality, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+von+Neumann+algebra"} commutative von Neumann algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is dual to a compact strictly localizable enhanced measurable space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            in the usual sense. Under this equivalence, the element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\in A
            corresponds to the measurable map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A\to \mathbf{C}
            given by inclusion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
          %p
            One may ask whether we can recover the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+theorem"} spectral theorem
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+operator"} normal operator
            in this manner. This is possible once
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+duality"} Stone duality
            is upgraded to Serre–Swan-type duality between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            and
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+modules"} sheaves of modules
            etc.).
          %p
            Given a
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\to S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            of maps
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\to k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\to S
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S=Spec A
            has as its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            over some point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in S
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi IM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M/IM
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            corresponding to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
          %p
            Typically, genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+modules"} dualizable modules
            (dualizable with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            over
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+modules"} sheaves of modules
            that are not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skyscraper+sheaves"} skyscraper sheaves
            etc.
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"}> vector bundle
                  \-like object
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} module over a Boolean algebra
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  sheaf of
                  = succeed "-vector" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Z}/2
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+W%2A-module"} Hilbert W*-module
                  over a commutative von Neumann algebra
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} measurable field of Hilbert spaces
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W%2A-representations"} W*-representations
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+von+Neumann+algebra"} commutative von Neumann algebra
                  on a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+field+of+Hilbert+spaces"} measurable field of Hilbert spaces
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+C%2A-module"} Hilbert C*-module
                  over a commutative unital C*-algebra
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} continuous field of Hilbert spaces
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                  over a commutative ring
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaf
                  of
                  = succeed "-modules" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒪
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+module"} dualizable module
                  over a commutative algebra over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} algebraic vector bundle
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  dualizable module over a finitely generated germ-determined C
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^\infty
                  \-ring
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} smooth vector bundle
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} dualizable module over finitely presented complex EFC-algebra
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} holomorphic vector bundle
          %p
            The duality relevant to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+theory"} spectral theory
            is the duality between representations of a commutative von Neumann algebras on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+fields"} measurable fields
            of Hilbert spaces.
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+operator"} normal operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            generates a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+von+Neumann+algebra"} commutative von Neumann algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            inside
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(H)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            is a compact strictly localizable enhanced measurable space.
          %p
            Furthermore, the inclusion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(H)
            is a representation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+field"} measurable field
            of Hilbert spaces over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+field"} measurable field
            produced by the classical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+theorem"} spectral theorem
          %p
            Under the duality, the operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            corresponds to the operator that multiplies a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+field"} measurable field
            of Hilbert spaces by the complex-valued function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A\to \mathbf{C}
            produced above. Thus, we recovered the entire content of the classical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+theorem"} spectral theorem
          %p
            In fact, the above considerations work equally well to establish the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+theorem"} spectral theorem
            for an arbitrary family (not necessarily finite) of commuting normal operators.
